; The first step of a frame's level: what multiplies the gain. Five cards a frame in: snd and V, the segment's kind,
; and loud's two loudnesses (for a voiced frame and for the breathy first one); two out, a mode and a factor for
; mulx. A silent frame: mode 3 (A is 0). A sonorant: mode 1 and the loudness of its vowel (the voiced one's, or with
; V 0 the next vowel's). Anything else: mode 0.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   snd      03-34: a frame: silent, a sonorant, or neither
  04                    INP   v
  05                    INP   kind
  06                    INP   lv
  07                    INP   lu
  08                    CLA   z
  09                    STO   y
  10                    STO   mode
  11                    CLA   snd
  12                    SUB   00
  13                    TAC   sil
  14                    SUB   00
  15                    TAC   snd1
  16            sil     CLA   n3
  17                    STO   mode
  18                    JMP   out
  19            snd1    CLA   kind
  20                    SUB   n2
  21                    TAC   out
  22                    SUB   00
  23                    TAC   son
  24                    JMP   out
  25            son     CLA   lv
  26                    STO   y
  27                    CLA   v
  28                    SUB   00
  29                    TAC   asp
  30                    JMP   one
  31            asp     CLA   lu
  32                    STO   y
  33            one     CLA   00
  34                    STO   mode
  35            out     OUT   mode
  36                    OUT   y
  37                    JMP   frm
  50            snd     DATA  0
  51            v       DATA  0
  52            kind    DATA  0
  53            lv      DATA  0
  54            lu      DATA  0
  55            y       DATA  0
  56            mode    DATA  0
  57            z       DATA  0
  58            n2      DATA  2
  59            n3      DATA  3
